On February 26, 2025, TKO Group Holdings, Inc. ("TKO") completed its acquisition of the Professional Bull Riders ("PBR"), On Location, and IMG businesses from Endeavor Group Holdings, Inc. ("Endeavor").

The total consideration paid by TKO at the transaction close was approximately **$3.25 billion**. This consideration was paid in the form of approximately **26.1 million** TKO Common Units (and an equivalent number of shares of TKO PubCo Class B Common Stock). The valuation was based on the 25-day volume-weighted average price (VWAP) of TKO’s Class A common stock ending on October 23, 2024. 

Additionally, the transaction included a purchase price adjustment settled in equity consisting of approximately **400,000** TKO Common Units, which had an aggregate value of **$50 million** at the time of the agreement.

FINAL ANSWER: The total consideration cost TKO paid to acquire the Endeavor assets (PBR, On Location, and IMG) measured at transaction close was approximately $3.25 billion, primarily consisting of 26.1 million TKO Common Units.

